meta {
  name: normalize regions
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{collection_url}}/internal/normalize-regions
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.scanned: isNumber
  res.body.normalized: isNumber
  res.body.skipped: isNumber
}

docs {
  Nightly lever (second step of the collection-rematch CronJob's
  chain, after normalize-platforms and ahead of the entry rematch so a
  just-promoted region's pricing class corrects in the same run),
  operator-runnable any time: promotes free-text entry regions into
  the known set, exact-or-synonym folding only - never fuzzy, so an
  unreviewed string is left as typed. A game-backed entry additionally
  re-picks its release date and localized snapshot for the promoted
  region from a fresh product fetch - the same pick resnapshot uses -
  so no follow-up resnapshot run is needed for those display fields;
  an enrichment outage skips that row for the next run rather than
  failing the whole sweep. Idempotent: a promoted row leaves the
  selection set. Expect 200 with scanned/normalized/skipped.

  Guard: admin role or a service token. The bearer behind
  {{access_token}} must be an admin - the folder's dev-token flow logs
  in as alice by default, so run it with body {"user": "admin"} first,
  or override --env-var access_token with a minted admin or service
  token.
}
